cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "magma-1518-obstruction-lean: one-generated (1518 + 3862)-magmas are trivial or the Z/3 shift, and constant-coefficient magma cohomology cannot refute 1518 => 47, 614, 817, 3862"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Perassi
    given-names: Carlo
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
url: https://github.com/carlok/magma-1518-obstruction-lean
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 (core, no axioms) proof that in any magma satisfying ETP laws 1518 and 3862 the set {x, x*x, (x*x)*(x*x)}
  carries the multiplication table of the cyclic shift, so one-generated such magmas are trivial or the Z/3 shift
  (a conjecture of T. Tao, Nov 2024, in a stronger form); kernel-checked certificates that every 1518-cocycle over
  the shift with finite fibre is a coboundary; hence constant-coefficient abelian extensions of finite 1518-magmas
  never refute 1518 => 47, 614, 817, 3862. Also an explicit family of finite 1518-magmas of sizes 3|M| violating
  47, 614, 817, 3862, over any ring with 1/2 and a square root of -1 (Lean kernel-checked members of sizes 15 and 39),
  and the classification of base-dependent extensions of the Z/3 shift: refuting ones exist over F_p iff p = 1 mod 4
  (exhaustive to p = 61, Groebner bases to p = 257). Automated proofs by Vampire, census by Mace4, z3 and Lean bv_decide.
